# Boundary display update, 9 October 2026.
# Main context strokes are clipped to the visible country-fill footprint.
# The southern Ilemi baseline follows the supplied FAO reference map; its
# endpoints are taken from the supplied Ilemi line, with a horizontal latitude.
# This baseline is a display convention only, not a change to country polygons.
# Exact WGS84 line coordinates embedded from the supplied
# UN_Disputed_areas_Africa.zip (19 features, four shapefiles).
# Reference: supplied UN Map No. 4651 Rev.4, July 2026, and FAO map examples.
# https://design-system.qa.fao.org/docs/interactive/maps/
# https://data.apps.fao.org/static/disclaimers/disclaimer.html
# This implements the supplied disputed-line convention, not a certification
# of every GADM boundary. Prediction values/aggregation are unchanged.
# IMPORTANT: the original averaging of interval endpoints below does not
# produce pooled posterior or administrative-area credible intervals.
#
# No extra download, TIFF, ZIP or shapefile is required at run time.
# Fills keep their original polygons. Solid international strokes are separated
# from fills; short solid transitions reconnect to supplied dashed endpoints.
# Internal district/region borders are retained outside a 100 m national-edge
# separation tolerance. No supplied dashed line is extended or moved.
# The 12 km display corridor accommodates differing UN/GADM generalisation
# (the supplied Ilemi line differs from GADM 4.1 by up to about 9.3 km).
# Only line drawing changes, never point assignment or prevalence values.
# Multipart borders are normalised before splitting: casting a mixed
# LINESTRING/MULTILINESTRING vector directly can discard all but its first part.
# Endpoint repairs are bounded by twice the display tolerance; small offshore
# rings are excluded from endpoint snapping to avoid spurious connections.
boundary_display_crs <- "+proj=laea +lat_0=8 +lon_0=39 +datum=WGS84 +units=m +no_defs"
boundary_display_tolerance_m <- 12000
boundary_disclaimer <- paste(
  ""
)

